            "result_text": "Done! I've created a regex pattern that:\n\n1. **Validates IPv4 addresses** without leading zeros using a 4-part octet pattern:\n   - `25[0-5]` for 250-255\n   - `2[0-4]\\d` for 200-249  \n   - `1\\d{2}` for 100-199\n   - `[1-9]?\\d` for 0-99\n\n2. **Matches dates** in YYYY-MM-DD format with:\n   - Months: 01-12\n   - Days: 01-31 (February allowed up to 29)\n\n3. **Selects the last date** on each line using a negative lookahead that prevents matching if another date follows\n\n4. **Prevents false matches** with word boundaries (`(?<!\\w)` and `(?!\\w)`) to ensure dates and IPv4s aren't preceded/followed by alphanumeric characters\n\nThe single capturing group ensures `re.findall()` returns only the dates, one per matching line."
